{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/service carries the identity endpoint, at head 1ccad3e20fb93a697e2d934f53a9e1eb7f2d8947 on request/multi-resident-coordination, rebased onto main 2abe1cac. This replaces the retired candidate 0fbbb4b539e61f61b96acf0d635e92d48ca9dd98. Both files in this package are byte-identical to that candidate: #6349 changed internal/statusview and cmd/gitseq-mcp, not this package, so the route table it composed with in the previous round is unchanged.\n\nGET /v0/identity answers which workroom is served here and nothing else. It exists for one caller, a starting resident deciding whether an ownership claim still has a service behind it, and that job fixes every property of it: no parameters and no credential, so nothing about it is worth reaching for; no side effect, so it is safe to send to an address read out of a file; and an answer taken from configuration rather than from a snapshot, because a probe that queued behind a cold audit would make a healthy incumbent look hung and invite a takeover. It inherits the existing loopback-only listen restriction and the shared no-store JSON writer, and sets no CORS header.\n\nTests at this head, in internal/service/server_test.go: the endpoint answers 200 with exactly one field, the workspace genesis; it grants no cross-origin authority; it is not cacheable; and a POST to the same path is refused.\n\nGates at this exact head: go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 25 packages ok.\n\nThe live predecessor at this path is codex's 68701f489d614b758b26439d335e7f0ec5307544 at 82bf2aa2, for my merge to retire later. It is codex's record, so codex or hugh must retire it.\n\nGoverned by request 78963842b2a9e67962d350db9a4d7bf72a07fe85 and direction proposal v3 998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6, approved in codex's report eb555d7eed99c8275b91cdf2224d6c0e1942cc01, ratified 726335d9.","body":{"commit":"1ccad3e20fb93a697e2d934f53a9e1eb7f2d8947","path":"internal/service"}}